      "x": -250,
      "y": -1120,
      "width": 500,
      "height": 230,
      "text": "# P\u0101t\u0101l\n\nGarment pattern CAD \u2014 idea to production-ready pattern in one workspace.\n\n> Every operation here is either correct or loud. A pattern piece that is silently wrong is worse than one that refuses to compute: the first gets cut out of cloth, the second gets fixed.\n\n`engine/crates/geometry/src/lib.rs` \u00b7 build with `scripts\\cargo.bat` \u00b7 [docs index](README.md)",
      "color": "#6c7bd1"
    },
    {
      "id": "live_status",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": -800,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 660,
      "text": "**Live \u00b7 status.md** \u2014 single source of truth. If it disagrees with any other note, it wins.\n\n![[status]]"
    },
    {
      "id": "live_work",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 260,
      "y": -800,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 660,
      "text": "**Live \u00b7 remaining-work.md** \u2014 what is left, in order, and what blocks what. Ticked as work lands.\n\n![[remaining-work]]"
    },
    {
      "id": "gate_freeze",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 260,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "## \u26d4 The gate \u2014 v2 shape freeze\n\nChunk A. Roughly twenty minutes, and a one-way door: once the migration is written against a shape, changing the shape means changing the migration. **Task 8 must not start without an explicit sign-off.**\n\nUnblocks Chunk B, plus grading and pattern primitives in D.\n\nLoad-bearing reading to confirm: freezing v2 does *not* decide whether a dart is an object \u2014 a dart is an additive field either way.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "risk_c",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -780,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 520,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "## \u26d4 The highest-risk gap \u2014 Chunk C\n\nThe validations that can say *the software is wrong*. Needs no Mac and no code, and has not moved while the engine moved a great deal.\n\nThe calibration page has never been printed and no pattern maker has been found \u2014 the two tests that count.\n\nK3 (draft a block in Seamly2D *and* Freesewing) is the critical path to Decision 2 and to ADR-006.",
      "color": "1"
    },
